2 CONT YDNA Descendants of
2 CONT Capitan Marcos Alonso GARZA ARCON
2 CONT First 10 Generations
2 CONT
2 CONT by Crispin.Rendon
2 CONT
2 CONT There are over 114,000 descendants of Marcos Alonso Garza Arcon in our kindred database
2 CONT and of those over 3,700 carry his yDNA. Many but not all males with the surnames Falcon,
2 CONT Garza, Montemayor and Trevino are Y-DNA descendants of Marcos Alonso. The surname
2 CONT Garza Arcon is unique. Some have espoused that Garza Arcon should be Garza Falcon as used
2 CONT my Blas Garza Falcon. Three of Marcos' sons took their mother's surname Trevino (seen rarely
2 CONT as Temino). The surname Montemayor sprouts four generations later. This is a very different
2 CONT YDNA line then that of Diego Montemayor (founder of Monterrey) whose YDNA line died
2 CONT hundreds of years ago. Marcos Alonso's Y-DNA haplogroup is understood to be R-M269 and
2 CONT after Big Y DNA testing is now known as R-BY15969. Thanks to the efforts of David Reta and
2 CONT the FTDNA Garza DNA project for continued research with this ancestral line.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familytreedna.com/groups/garza/about
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally a word about the small town of Lepe, Spain where Marcos Alonso was born. When you
2 CONT tell someone from Spain that your ancestor was from Lepe they may smile expecting that you
2 CONT are joking, the reason being that Lepe is famous in Spain for being the subject of jokes.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Capitan Marcos Alonso GARZA ARCON, born in Lepe, Huelva, Spain, son of Marcos
2 CONT ALONSO. He married in Mexico City, D.F., Mexico.
2 CONT  Children of Capitan Marcos Alonso GARZA ARCON were as follows:
2 CONT + 2 i Capitan Alonso TREVINO, died Dec 1654 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT He married (1); (2); (3).
2 CONT + 3 ii Capitan Pedro GARZA, died 8 Feb 1639 in Salinas Victoria, Nuevo Leon,
2 CONT Mexico. He married (1); (2).
2 CONT + 4 iii Marcos Alonso GARZA, died Dec 1654. He married.
2 CONT + 5 iv Capitan Blas GARZA FALCON, died 21 Feb 1669 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon,
2 CONT Mexico, buried 21 Feb 1669 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico. He married.
2 CONT + 6 v Capitan Diego TREVINO. He married.
2 CONT + 7 vi Capitan Francisco GARZA. He married (1); (2).
2 CONT + 8 vii Caudillo Joseph TREVINO, died 12 Nov 1646 in Apodaca, Nuevo Leon,
2 CONT Mexico. He married (1); (2). 
2 CONT
