2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/cavazos.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT En 1642 el Gobernador del Nuevo Reino de León, Martín de Zavala, confirmó los títulos de la hacienda de Santo Domingo del capitán Juan Cavazos quien logró extender su territorio a lo que desde 1836 es el municipio de San Nicolás d
2 CONC e los Garza, Nuevo León. 
2 CONT
2 CONT English summary: Gov. Martin de Zavala confirms land grant. Since 1836, this is known as the Municipality of San Nicolas de los Garza, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Cavazos
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a son named Fray Juan Cavazos
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT * Juan Cavazos del Campo ca 1605-1683
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Origin and family Born in 1605 in the town of Santa Maria, Old Castile, Spain. Son of Giovanni Cavazzi, Carnico Cavazzo native province of Udine, Italy and Simona Del Campo of Spanish origin. He came to the New Kingdom of León in 
2 CONC 1628. He married Elena de la Garza Rodriguez in 1627, daughter of Pedro de la Garza Falcon and Maria Ines Rodriguez Trevino Guajardo, with whom he had nine children: John, Margaret, Anthony, Clara, Mary, Lucy, Joseph, Gabriel and 
2 CONC Pablo Cavazos of Garza. For some reason, the daughters were registered with the maternal surname first, ie, "de la Garza Cavazos". His works He was responsible for the parish church that existed on the site now occupied by the Cat
2 CONC hedral of Monterrey, compared to Marco and the old Monterrey City Hall. Captain Juan Cavazos the first builder of Nuevo Leon that has been reported. On 4 occasions was mayor of the city of Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico (formerly M
2 CONC etropolitan City of Our Lady of Monterrey in Nuevo Leon, New Spain) in 1647, 1666, 1669, 1676. In 1642 the Governor of Nuevo Leon, Martin de Zavala, confirmed the titles of the estate of Santo Domingo of Captain Juan Cavazos who w
2 CONC as able to extend its territory which since 1836 is the municipality of San Nicolas de los Garza, Nuevo Leon. The grant of the lands of what is now San Nicolas de los Garza dates from February 5, 1597. The name CAVAZOS Captain Jua
2 CONC n Cavazos is what gave rise to the name Cavazos in northern Mexico and southern Texas. Because in those days there was the conflict with the United States and Mexico lost part of its territory and after the French invasion, they d
2 CONC ecided hispanize also their surnames and avoid being confused with the French and changed their names. Thereby Cavazzi became Cavazos. In the oldest documents available, dating from 5 to April 13, 1628, concerning the will of John
2 CONC  Cavazos, appears as a resident of Royal and Minas de San Gregorio (now Township Cerralvo, Texas). Both documents signed as John Cabasso. In testimony signed by a notary public wrote his name as Jhoan Cavacos although in the same 
2 CONC document is also written Cabasso. In these documents the reverse bears the legend: "1635 Letter Juo Cavasos my dowry." although signed documents as John Cabassos. His eldest son, Fray Juan Cavazos, a Catholic priest of the Order o
2 CONC f St. Francis of Assisi in Monterrey, and signed as "John Cavasos". His death The June 15, 1683, Captain Juan Cavazos died, was buried in the Convent of San Francisco in Monterrey and the Hacienda de Santo Domingo was in charge of
2 CONC  his sons Antonio and Jose Cavazos captains. References   "Biographical Dictionary of Monterrey Builders" by Juan Roberto Zavala Index to the Marriage Investigations of the Diocese of Guadalajara - Provinces of Coahuila - Nuevo Le
2 CONC on - Nuevo Santander - Texas, Volume Two: 1751-1779, 1997
