1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  I'm a direct descendant of this couple (through 2 of their sons including the one that they say is Marcos Alonso Arcon)and I'm also a direct descendant of Marcos Alonso. Their trees simply don't meet. He is defini
2 CONC tely not their son. DO NOT REMOVE
2 CONT
2 CONT NONE OF THE FOLLOWING NARRATIVE INDICATES ANYTHING ABOUT THIS MAN BEING THE SON OF ANA ESTRADA CABALLERIA AND HER HUSBAND
2 CONT   Juan GÓMEZ GALLARDO LATAPÍ's Family Tree
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana  ESTRADA DE-LA-CABALLERÍA Sosa/Ahnentafel # 81,133 Family Tree Profile Matches Print Illustrated family tree Family Ancestry Charts & lists Family tree Check Descendants Lists Family tree Relationship Calculate relationship Re
2 CONC lationship with x x (Sosa/Ahnentafel #1) Relationship with Juan Alonso CABRERA (spouse) More Illustrated statistics   Map   Set as family tree root F  Ana ESTRADA DE-LA-CABALLERÍAPrint Family TreeSosa : 81,133 Born in 1492 Decease
2 CONC d - Nueva Galicia, México
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents Alonso ESTRADA DE-LA-CABALLERÍA Mariana GUTIÉRREZ FLORES-DE-LA-CABALLERIA
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses and children Married to Juan Alonso CABRERA †1564 (Parents : Lope SOSA †1520 & Inés CABRERA) with F María SOSA CABRERA M Lope SOSA † married to Inés CASTILLA-OSORIO SOSA M Juan Alonso ESTRADA 1542- married to Mariana GUEVA
2 CONC RA BARRIOS
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gw5.geneanet.org/sanchiz?lang=en;pz=tomas;nz=sanchez+garza;ocz=0;p=marcos;n=alonso  ...  In David T. Raphael's book ''The Cinonquistadores and Crypto-Jews of Monterrey'', page 189, Constanza's daughter submitted The Genealo
2 CONC gy of the Garzas as given by Elvira Sanchez (previously Elvira de la Garza) in a 1570 deposition to the Inquisition. She stated that her father was Pedro de Lepe, born and reared in Lepe. Her mother, of course, was Constanza de la
2 CONC  Garza, born in Condado de Lepe, and a resident of the isle of Grand Canary. Her body was burned in the auto de fe in the Canary Island of La Palma in 1526, after she had already died while under house arrest. Her paternal grandfa
2 CONC ther's surname was Vizcaino. Her grandmother was Elvira Alonso from condado de Lepe. Her maternal grandparents were Hernan Garza de la Garza and Beatris Nuñes both from Sevilla.  Her maternal uncles were Alonso de la Garza, who di
2 CONC ed in the Canaries [burned by the Inquisition in the auto de fe of 1526] father of Hernando and Francisco and two daughters. Her siblings were Beatriz Sanchez, Ysabel Sanchez, Ana Luysa, Francisco Sanchez, and Diego de Lepe. N.B. 
2 CONC The above Constanza, therefore, could not have been the mother of Constanza de la Garza born in 1529. It is possible that the younger Constanza is a relative.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Correct spelling is ARCON.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The following text explains the possible reasons for the name change from de Arcon to de la Garza.  It also documents the land grand request which I've cut and pasted below for quicker reference.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcos Alonso Garza y Arcon
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcos Alonso Garza y Arcon was born in 1562 in Lepe, Huelva, a city located in the province of Castile in Spain. He died in 1634. He married Juana de Treviño Quintanilla who was born 1566 in Mexico City. Marcos and Juana married 
2 CONC about 1580 in Durango. The migration to north to Northern Mexico had begun and great progress had been made. Durango is hundreds of miles removed from Mexico City.
2 CONT
2 CONT They procreated six sons. Captain Pedro, Captain Blas and Francisco took on the surname of de la Garza. Captain Alonso, Diego and Commander Joseph took on the surname of de Treviño.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here the Treviño surname takes a twist. The paternal line is not followed by Joseph, Captain Alonso and Diego. They instead chose their mother's surname. This may have been done for inheritance purposes or to carry on a name they 
2 CONC felt was illustrious and merited perpetuity. So again, if the truth is told and convention is followed, the descendants of Joseph de Treviño through whom I have established my maternal-paternal line are in fact de la Garza y Arcon
2 CONC , not Treviño. The conclusion that can therefore be reached is that most Treviños, Ayalas and Garza are all descendants of Marcos Alonso Garza y Arcon. Some scholars believe that Arcon is an archaic word for Falcon. Again, the mix
2 CONC  begins to get worse. The name Falcon gets merged into the group of descendants of Marcos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Francisco de Urdiñola, appointed as governor and captain of Nueva Viscaya, sent a memorandum-book dated 1604 to the king of Spain. Captain Urdiñola lists two of the bachelor sons of Marcos Alonso as inhabitants of Real y M
2 CONC inas of Cuencame, probably. Although Urdiñola does not list their names. In the intervening years, Captain Marcos Alonso Garza lived in the town of Santiago de Saltillo. On May 30, 1610, he solicited from Captain Diego de Rodrigue
2 CONC z, deputy to the governor of Nuevo Reino de Leon, various gifts of land and water in the vicinity of the town of Cerralvo and ownership of the "Borrado" Indians. He received this grant. In one of his petitions, he writes: "I have 
2 CONC come with Captain Diego Rodriguez, deputy to the governor by the king our Lord, with my arms and horses for whatever might be needed…." [Civil Registry, volume 26, 1703, file 4, folio 53. MAM. To date, it is the oldest known docum
2 CONC ent which has Marcos Alsonso's signature affixed to it. He or a son of the same name served as alderman in the municipal government of Monterrey in 1612 and 1616. In the list of inhabitants of Nuevo Reino de Leon dated 1626, Capta
2 CONC in Alonso Marcos de Garza does not appear. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.villadan.com/webcards/ps03/ps03_002.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT LAND GRANT REQUEST TEXT FROM ABOVE:
2 CONT
2 CONT "I have come with Captain Diego Rodriguez, deputy to the governor by the king our Lord, with my arms and horses for whatever might be needed…." [Civil Registry, volume 26, 1703, file 4, folio 53. MAM. See VillaDan. com Webcard lin
2 CONC k above.
2 CONT --------------------
