2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Conquistador of Nuevo Santander, he was born in Castile, Spain. By 1733, Captain Antonio Ladrón de Guevara was a resident of Nuevo León, México and during his first 12 years in Nuevo León he undertook expeditions through the state
2 CONC s of Nuevo León, Coahuila, and Texas. In 1739, he wrote of his account of the ranches, settlements, missions, and Spanish frontier policy. The guidebook served in planning defenses on the northern frontier and in changing local ad
2 CONC ministration. Ladrón de Guevara also helped the expedition of José de Escandón for the pacification and settlement of Nuevo Santander, which, together with Nuevo León, Coahuila, and Texas, formed the Provincias Internas de Oriente
2 CONC . Among the Texas sites he described were the presidios of San Juan Bautista and San Antonio de Bexar (San Antonio, Texas). His analysis of the role of Texas in the frontier defensive cordon is of great interest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Index to the Marriage Investigations of the Diocese of Guadalajara, by Raul J. Guerra, Jr., Nadine M. Vasquez, and Baldomero Vela, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Presidio and Militia on the Northern Frontier of New Spain, Volume Two, Part Two, by Diana Hadley, Thomas H. Naylor, & Mardith K. Schuetz-Miller, eds. (Research):http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/garza.htm&nbsp; n.58
