1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 69. JUANA4 DE CEPEDA-DE-LA-FUENTE (JUANA3 DE-LA-FUENTE-MARTINEZ, FRANCISCA2 MARTINEZ-GUAJARDO-NAVARRO-RODRIGUEZ, JUAN-FRANCISCO1 MARTINEZ-GUAJARDO) died in Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico. She married (1) CAPTAIN BERNAR
2 CONC DO DE-LOS-SANTOS-COY-DE-LA-CERDA in Saltillo, Coahulia, Mexico, son of BERNARDO DE-LOS-SANTOS-COY and MARIA-INES DE-LA-CERDA-Y-CASTRO. He died October 25, 1676 in Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico. She married (2) CAPTAIN ANTONIO DE VALC
2 CONC ARCEL-SOTOMAYOR-Y-RIVADENEYRA in Saltillo, Coahulia, Mexico. He was born in Michoacan, Mexico, and died Abt. April 15, 1678 in Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JUANA DE CEPEDA-DE-LA-FUENTE:
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Origen de los Fundadores de Texas, Nuevo Mexico, Coahulia, y Nuevo Leon, by Guillermo Garmendia Leal. (page 132).
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for CAPTAIN BERNARDO DE-LOS-SANTOS-COY-DE-LA-CERDA:
2 CONT
2 CONT On October 23, 1676, he signed his last will and testament. Source:Origen de los Fundadores de Texas, Nuevo Mexico, Coahulia, y Nuevo Leon, by Guillermo Garmendia Leal. Page 77 & 132.
2 CONT
