1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cavazos Garza, Israel.  ''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700'', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, page
2 CONC s 142-143, #456 [V, fol. 170v., no.92].  ...  This protocolo sets forth the '''will of Capitán Francisco Botello de Morales'''.  He states that he's the legitimate son of Pedro Botello de Morales and Ama María de Avila, both decea
2 CONC sed and that his father was a native of Valverde, Extremadura, Spain, and that his mother was a native of the city of Códova, Spain.  He stipulates burial in the "Parroquial", then sets forth his debts.  He states that he married 
2 CONC Juana de la Garza, legitimate daughter of Marcos Alonso de la Garza and Catalina Martínez Guajardo, who were residents of Saltillo. He identifies his children Sebastián, María, Diego, Melchora, Pedro, Petrona, Juan, and Francisca-
2 CONC -all adults. Then he allocates inheritances and states that María will marry José de la Serna, Melchora is to marry Andrés González, Petronila to marry Diego Galván, and Francisca now married to Juan Bautista de Saldúa,  ...  '''M
2 CONC onterrey, 16 April 1696''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''__________________________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendents of Captain Pedro Botello de Morales
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. CAPTAIN FRANCISCO4 BOTELLO-DE-MORALES (PEDRO3, UNKNOWN2 BUENTELLO-GUERRERO, BOTELLO1 BUENTELLO) was born 1615, and died April 17, 1696 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico. He married JUANA DE-LA-GARZA-MARTINEZ-GUAJARDO Abt. 1635, 
2 CONC daughter of MARCOS-ALONSO DE-LA-GARZA-Y-ARCON and CATALINA MARTINEZ-GUAJARDO. She was born Abt. 1615 in Mapimi, Durango, Mexico, and died January 27, 1693/94 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/botello.htm
