1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Juan de OLIVARES [60] 
2 CONT *was born in 1590 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, New Spain. 
2 CONT *He died on 20 October 1669 at the age of 79 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, New Spain. He was buried in Cathedral, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, New Spain. 
2 CONT *Parents: Diego de OLIVARES and ______ ______ (spouse of Diego de Olivares).
2 CONT *Spouse: Juana de TREVIÑO. Juana de TREVIÑO and Juan de OLIVARES were married in 1625. Children were: 
2 CONT **1. Joseph de OLIVARES, 
2 CONT **2. Diego de OLIVARES, 
2 CONT **3. Blas de OLIVARES, 
2 CONT **4. Bartolome de OLIVARES, 
2 CONT **5. Alonso de OLIVARES, 
2 CONT **6. Beatrice OLIVARES de Treviño, 
2 CONT **7. Juana de OLIVARES, 
2 CONT **8. Anastacia de OLIVARES.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b167.html#P1089
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From Los Origens De La Familia Olivares by Zacarias Joel Olivarez (webcached 2/2/2013):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/o/l/i/Zacarias--J-Olivarez/index.html
2 CONT
2 CONT General General Juan De Olivares (b. Abt. 1605, d. 20 Oct 1669)
2 CONT
2 CONT General Juan De Olivares (son of Diego De Olivares and Maria Gonzalez) 
2 CONT *was born Abt. 1605 in Mexico City Mexico, and 
2 CONT *died 20 Oct 1669 in Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico. 
2 CONT *He married Juana De Trevino on 1625 in Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **daughter of Joseph De Trevino and Sebastiana Garcia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan De Olivares came to Nuevo Leon with Diego Rodriguez ABT 1618. He received a citation on June 7, 1624 from Diego Rodriguez for helping with the hostile indians in Cerralvo Mexico. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan De Olivares' ranch was named EL RANCHO DE SAN ANTONIO. It was located at Pescaria Chica Lake. He also had a Hacienda which he called Magdalena where he grew wheat. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When he became a soldier, he had no capital or influence, but he was a good soldier as witnessed by the citations he received during his service. He raised to the rank of General. He discovered mines and worked them profitably. He
2 CONC  was granted his land by the then Governor Zavala in 1635. He built a dam and canals, but he accidently built it on his brother-in-law's (Alonso Trevino) land and as a result of a suit, lost the Dam and the canals on July 4, 1656.
2 CONC  He did get water rights from lake Pescaria Chica to irrigate his wheat at his Hacienda Magdalena. He was the first man to grow wheat in the New World. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on October 20, 1669 and is buried in the catherdal grounds in Monterrey.He had a house in Monterrey which he gave to Juan Bautista Chapa who married Beatriz, his daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana, his wife, died July 2, 1693
2 CONT
2 CONT More About General Juan De Olivares and Juana De Trevino:
2 CONT *Marriage: 1625, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of General Juan De Olivares and Juana De Trevino are:
2 CONT *1. +Joseph De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1626, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1675, Mier Mexico.
2 CONT *2. Diego De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1630, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT *3. Blas De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1632, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. 12 Jun 1677, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico.
2 CONT *4. +Juan De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1634, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1698, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico.
2 CONT *5. +Bartolome De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 1644, Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1715, Nuevo Leon Mexico.
2 CONT *6. Antonio De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1646, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT *7. Juana De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1650, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT *8. Anastacia De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1652, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT *9. +Alonso De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1657, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1695, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico.
2 CONT *10. +Beatriz Trevino De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 1630, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1685, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico.
2 CONT --------------------
