1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Los Origens De La Familia Olivares by Zacarias Joel Olivarez (webcached 2/2/2013):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/o/l/i/Zacarias--J-Olivarez/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0044.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Bartolome De Olivares (b. 1644, d. Abt. 1715)
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolome De Olivares (son of General Juan De Olivares and Juana De Trevino) 
2 CONT *was born 1644 in Nuevo Leon Mexico, and 
2 CONT *died Abt. 1715 in Nuevo Leon Mexico. 
2 CONT *He married Maria De Sepulveda De Benavides on 25 Dec 1673 in Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, daughter of Lazaro De Benavides.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolome De Olivares was the sixth child of General Juan De Olivares and Juana De Trevino. His brothers and sisters were as follows
2 CONT *1. Beatrice	1620
2 CONT *2. Joseph	1626
2 CONT *3. Diego	 1630
2 CONT *4. Blas	 1632
2 CONT *5. Juan	 1634
2 CONT *6. BARTOLOME	1644
2 CONT *7. Antonio	1646 (His closest brother in age)
2 CONT *8. Juana	
2 CONT *9. Anastacia	1652
2 CONT *10. Alfonso	1657
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears that Antonio and Bartolome had a very close relationship. They both can be found together in must that is found about them. They both joined the Escandon Expedition, they both got land grants close to each other, and co
2 CONC mbined their ranches at one time to combine and constitute the biggest cattle ranch in this newly settled area of the New World.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolome married Maria De Benavides De Sepulveda on Christmas Day, December 25, 1673 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico. She was from a family that had Aristocratic standing in Spain before migrating to the New World. They had four
2 CONC  children and they were
2 CONT *1.	Blas De Olivares, (named after his brother that died at an early age)
2 CONT *2.	Maria De Olivares
2 CONT *3.	Juan De Olivares
2 CONT *4.	Nicolas De Olivares
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Bartolome De Olivares and Maria De Sepulveda De Benavides are:
2 CONT *1. Maria De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 31 Dec 1674, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1749, Cerralvo Mexico.
2 CONT *2. Juan Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 06 Sep 1677, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT *3. +Blas De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 03 Mar 1680, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1745, Saltillo Mexico.
2 CONT *4. Nicolasa De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 01 Sep 1682, Monterrey Nuevo Leon Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT --------------------
