1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gonzalez Direct Lines - Person Sheet  ...  http://www.currays.net/Gonzalez%20Web%20Project/ps04/ps04_028.htm  ...  '''Santos ROJO a founder of Saltillo'''  ...  Martha Duron Jimenez and Ignacio Narro Etchegaray: ''
2 CONC DICCIONARIO BIOGRAFICO DE SALTILLO'', May1995, page 152  ... " Santos ROJO, Died in 1610. Founder and vecino of Saltillo. Some authors indicate that he was of Basque origin, others that he was of Italian stock, using Roxo instead 
2 CONC of Rojo; other authors say that he was a creole [born in Mexico of Spanish blood] and that his roots were in el Bajio. Others say that he was the son of Capitan Francisco ROJO who accompanied Hernan CORTES in the conquest of the S
2 CONC outheast. But it is certain that he participated in the founding of Saltilllo with Capitan Alberto del CANTO at the end of the decade of the 60’s [1560’s]. He married Dona Beatriz de las RUELAS. They were the parents of Juana, who
2 CONC  used the name NAVARRO, possibly the second surname of Dona Beatriz de las RUELAS NAVARRO, rather than the ROJO of her father. She married Capitan Juan de UZCANGA GUARNIZO; they had no descendants. He left all of his estate to the
2 CONC  daughters of his sister Estefania: '''Maria, who married Martin NAVARRO and later Capitan Martin OCHOA de ELIZALDE'''; Estefania, who married Domingo GIL de LEYVA; and Beatriz who married Bernardo de los SANTOS COY. It is said th
2 CONC at Santos ROJO, a businessman, at a fair in Jalapa in on business, bought an image of the crucified Christ to bring to Saltillo where it is venerated and is known as the Senor de la Capilla [Lord of the Chapel.] On March of 1608, 
2 CONC he arrived with it and placed it in the Capilla de las Animas [Chapel of Souls] which he, himself, had built in the transept of the first parish church, on the side of the gospel, with its altar. In 1614, the priest Baldo CORTES, 
2 CONC first priest of Saltillo, gave possession to Dona Beatriz de las RUELAS, Santos ROJO’s widow, of burial space for her and her descendants. Santos ROJO died in 1610; his wife survived him until 1650. He is buried in the Capilla del
2 CONC  Santo Cristo [Chapel of the Holy Christ.]"
2 CONT
2 CONT '''_____________________________'''
2 CONT
