2 CONC ocolo is the '''will of Juan Bautista Cavazos'''.  He states that he was born in Monterrey, lives at the Santa Rosa Ranch, is the legitimate '''son of Juan Cavazos and María Jacinta Fernández''', is ill, wishes to be buried in the
2 CONC  Iglesia Parroquial of Monterrey, and sets forth some bequests.  He states that he was '''married to Rosa María González, legitimate daughter of Juan González and María Cantú of the San Jose Hacienda in Cadereyta''', and that thei
2 CONC r '''children''' are Juan Nepumoceno, María Rosalia, José Dimas, Juana, María Brígida, and José Patricio.  He states that he '''married a second time to María Rafaela de Ayala, legitimate daughter of Pedro de Ayala and María Guada
2 CONC lupe de la Garza''', and that their '''children''' are José Felipe, José Fernando, María Manuela, José Tomas, José Francisco, María Magdalena, and María Gertrudis.  He states that all the children of his 1st marriage now are marri
2 CONC ed.  Witnesses are named.  ...  '''''Paraje de las Adjuntas de Santa Rosa, primero de Junio de 1784'''''
